    "id": "train-6698",
    "question": "Marie has 98 unread messages on her phone. She decides to clear them by reading 20 messages a day. However, she also gets 6 new messages a day. How many days will it take her to read all her unread messages?",
    "gold": "7",
    "answer": "Marie will read 20 but gain 6 unread messages a day, so she will lower the number of messages by 20 - 6 = <<20-6=14>>14.\nThus, it will take her 98 / 14 = <<98/14=7>>7 days to read all her unread messages.\n#### 7"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many days it will take Marie to read all her unread messages, we need to consider both the messages she reads each day and the new messages she receives each day. Let's break it down step by step.\n\n1. **Initial number of unread messages**: Marie starts with 98 unread messages.\n2. **Messages read per day**: Marie reads 20 messages each day.\n3. **New messages received per day**: Marie receives 6 new messages each day.\n\nEach day, the net change in the number of unread messages is the number of messages she reads minus the number of new messages she receives. This can be expressed as:\n\\[ \\text{Net change per day} = 20 - 6 = 14 \\text{ messages} \\]\n\nThis means that each day, the number of unread messages decreases by 14. To find out how many days it will take for her to read all 98 messages, we divide the initial number of unread messages by the net change per day:\n\\[ \\text{Number of days} = \\frac{98}{14} = 7 \\]\n\nTherefore, it will take Marie \\(\\boxed{7}\\) days to read all her unread messages.",
